Meal preparation (@meal-preparation: 0, is #trail, #contains @meal-preparation-inputs, #contains @meal-preparation-solve, #contains @meal-preparation-acquire, #contains @meal-preparation-store) { r_21WM7WVKWGZFKZB2WTXWF97MBP
Use @nutrition-needs to set daily needs and Nutrients.lingua for exact food preparations. Follow @meal-preparation-inputs, @meal-preparation-solve, @meal-preparation-acquire, then @meal-preparation-store. Demeter minimizes continuous acquisition cost under your bounds. Inspect practical portions, palatability, and cooking decisions.
} r_21WM7WVKWGZFKZB2WTXWF97MBP

Extension @meal-preparation "lince.source" { dependencies [
   { uri "Nutrients.lingua" label "Measured composition" required true }
   { uri "Nutrition-needs.lingua" label "Daily adult references" required true }
   { uri "Farming.lingua" label "Species lifecycles" required true }
   { uri "farming/Production.lingua" label "Editable production examples" required true }
 ] }

Set the plan (@meal-preparation-inputs: 0, #part-of @meal-preparation) { r_6GHFWXA8EA34KMFT0A8Y6TFJCM
1. Choose the adult reference or manual targets, currency, start date, and period; begin with seven days.
2. Select exact preparations. Raw bean offers need an explicit purchased-to-usable conversion to supply cooked bean nutrition. Weigh an actual batch to measure yield.
3. Enter a separate personal offer Record per seller/package. Add a quantified #price assertion in the chosen currency. Record package mass, usable yield, seller, observation date, and source. Explicit zero price is valid; unknown price is not free.
4. Enter dated stock lots, expiry, and usable grams. Stock has zero additional purchase cost and finite availability.
5. Give each food optional daily, weekly, or period bounds. No minimum means zero; no maximum means unlimited; maximum zero excludes. Equal bounds fix an amount. Exclude allergens explicitly.
6. Constrain container volume only with measured volume per usable gram; weight alone does not determine pot capacity.
} r_6GHFWXA8EA34KMFT0A8Y6TFJCM

Solve and inspect (@meal-preparation-solve: 0, #part-of @meal-preparation) { r_6N1N417HF6MAF9KMZR1GFH8NSM
Require the selected nutrient bounds each day. Compute contributions from each food's stated measurement basis. Missing measurements contribute zero and stay flagged. Minimize acquisition cost with continuous nonnegative quantities.

Inspect quantities, achieved bounds, active limits, prices, and missing fields. Infeasible means no acceptable assignment: inspect conflicting requirements and change inputs deliberately. A relaxed diagnostic is not a valid plan. Karma may request a solve and route proposals through ordinary authorized actions.

Save the result with its input hash and source revisions. Editing targets, offers, stock, or templates makes it stale; solve again before accepting.

Small worked model: hypothetical A provides 100 kcal and 10 g protein per 100 g at 2 currency units; B provides 100 kcal and no protein at 1 unit. For daily minima of 200 kcal and 10 g protein, the minimum-cost quantities are 100 g A and 100 g B, costing 3 units. Capping A at 50 g makes the protein minimum infeasible. Replace these illustrative coefficients with the imported preparation measurements and your actual offers.

An authorized Karma action can request `{"action":"demeter","request":{"command":"solve","plan":"YOUR_PLAN_UID"}}`. Poll the returned run with `{"action":"demeter","request":{"command":"poll","run":"YOUR_RUN_UID"}}`. Review the result and dated task projection before the separate accept action. Generic linear models use the same action path with `"action":"optimize"`; neither action executes a purchase.
} r_6N1N417HF6MAF9KMZR1GFH8NSM

Acquire and grow (@meal-preparation-acquire: 0, #part-of @meal-preparation) { r_42Y7850M5CYDASTSQ1DTVDESXQ
Allocate available stock, then purchases or eligible expected harvests. After optimization, round each chosen offer upward to whole packages. Show continuous cost, rounded bill, and leftovers separately. Rounding may change the best checkout choice; this is not an integer checkout optimizer.

Choose buy or grow per food, or switch the whole plan to supermarket buying. Growing uses your declared usable-unit cost, confirmed yield, local season, and template. @lactuca-sativa supplies lettuce examples, @phaseolus-vulgaris beans, and @gallus-gallus-domesticus eggs. A future harvest cannot cover an earlier meal. Generate dated production inputs and buying gaps from recurring demand. Forecasts remain separate from inventory; count actual usable harvest before recording stock.
} r_42Y7850M5CYDASTSQ1DTVDESXQ

Cook, portion, cool, and review (@meal-preparation-store: 0, #part-of @meal-preparation) { r_6NRMKHHKQ6MAF9KMZR8HQN1P52
Batch compatible cooking methods, weigh usable output, and divide into labelled daily portions. Keep raw animal foods separate from ready-to-eat foods. Check safe internal temperatures for the food.

Cool promptly in shallow containers. Refrigerate within two hours, or one hour above 32°C. Keep the refrigerator at 4°C or colder and freezer at −18°C or colder. Most cooked leftovers keep 3–4 days refrigerated; freeze later portions of a seven-day plan promptly. Thaw safely; reheat leftovers to 74°C. Keep dates and storage conditions with each stock lot.

Record actual bill, usable yield, waste, portion acceptance, and harvest. Update the next plan from measurements.

[USDA leftovers](https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/leftovers-and-food-safety); [cold storage chart](https://www.foodsafety.gov/food-safety-charts/cold-food-storage-charts); [cooking temperatures](https://www.foodsafety.gov/food-safety-charts/safe-minimum-internal-temperatures).
} r_6NRMKHHKQ6MAF9KMZR8HQN1P52
